Zstandard 1.5.7 -- the decompressor only, for Onyx's NetSurf
===========================================================

Source: https://github.com/facebook/zstd/releases/download/v1.5.7/zstd-1.5.7.tar.gz
(sha256 eb33e51f49a15e023950cd7825ca74a4a2b43db8354825ac24fc1b7ee09e6fa3), BSD licence
(LICENSE; zstd is dual BSD / GPLv2, the BSD terms are the ones used here).

Kept: lib/zstd.h, lib/zstd_errors.h, lib/common/ (the headers, and entropy_common.c,
error_private.c, fse_decompress.c, zstd_common.c, xxhash.c, debug.c), lib/decompress/ (its .c
and .h, not the x86-64 assembly huf_decompress_amd64.S). Not kept: the compressor, the
dictionary builder, the legacy formats, the multithreading, the programs and tests.

No change to the sources. Built by user/netsurf/Makefile into libzstddec.a (committed, as the
other libraries) with -DZSTD_DISABLE_ASM -DZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=0 -DDEBUGLEVEL=0
-DZSTD_NO_TRACE; the PC bench (tools/tests/netsurf/host.mk) compiles the same files.

Used by user/netsurf/onyx_fetch.c: Content-Encoding: zstd, streamed (ZSTD_decompressStream),
a window of 8 MB at most (ZSTD_d_windowLogMax 23, as Chrome). About 70 KB of code on the Pi.
